# Codegen: prefer reusable helpers first

When adding or changing language generators (`crates/codegen*`, `crates/codegen-*`):

1. Before emitting a new per-model or per-edge helper, check whether a shared generic/runtime helper already exists — or extract one if the same body would be copied.
2. Prefer **one shared implementation + thin typed wrappers** over copy-pasted function bodies in generated output.
3. Only duplicate bodies when the logic is truly entity-specific (e.g. edge `RELATE` create).
4. Keep public named APIs stable when thinning internals unless the user explicitly asks to break them.
